## 17. Implementation Requirements

Build a real, working application, not a static UI prototype.

Do not use:
- Dummy data as a substitute for database integration
- Fake login functionality
- Hardcoded users
- Hardcoded workflow columns
- Mock CRUD operations
- Placeholder buttons
- In-memory-only task persistence

All important operations must work with Supabase.

Implement:

1. Authentication and protected routes.
2. Admin and Member permissions.
3. User CRUD and profile picture uploads.
4. App CRUD and icon uploads.
5. App version and update history.
6. Board CRUD.
7. Dynamic workflow columns.
8. Task CRUD and drag-and-drop.
9. Task assignments.
10. App-to-task relationships.
11. Comments and attachments.
12. My Tasks page.
13. Overview page.

Ensure loading, error, empty, and success states are implemented.

